{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778976055110,"sessionID":"ses_1ccc3b105ffeGJVZ03NDbrWwnP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_VtG3JmtDMN5C3lbrAWPx6CLU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":2000},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\n- CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n- CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nCD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\n- exhausted CD4 T cell\\n- CD4+ exhausted T lymphocyte\\n- exhausted CD4-positive T cell\\n\\nCD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\n- exhausted CD8 T cell\\n- CD8+ exhausted T lymphocyte\\n- exhausted CD8-positive T cell\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nCD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\nA CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation(e.g., chronic infection, tumors, or persistent inflammation). This state is characterised by sustained expression of PD-1 as a shared feature. Additional exhaustion-associated molecules, including the transcription factor TOX, and context- or stage-dependent changes in markers such as LAG-3, TIM-3, CD39, and T-bet, may also be observed; however, the expression levels of these molecules vary depending on exhaustion stage and tissue environment.\\n(PMID:31390978; PMID:31207603; PMID:36907685; PMID:38166256)\\n\\nCD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\nA CD8-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation (e.g., chronic infection, tumours, or persistent inflammation). This state is characterised by sustained expression of PD-1 as a shared feature. Additional exhaustion-associated molecules, including expression of the transcription factor TOX and reduced T-bet, and context- or stage-dependent changes in markers such as LAG-3, TIM-3, CD39, and EOMES, may also be observed; however, the expression levels of these molecules vary depending on exhaustion stage and disea... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-87UJcoB\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"scheuerm\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n10:       \"body\": \"Rather than \\\"A CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation under chronic antigenic stimulation\\\" I would recommend \\\"A CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation **_as a result_** of chronic antigenic stimulation\\\"\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-20T17:31:29Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [\n16:         {\n17:           \"content\": \"THUMBS_UP\",\n18:           \"users\": {\n19:             \"totalCount\": 1\n20:           }\n21:         }\n22:       ],\n23:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3453#issuecomment-3559246337\",\n24:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n25:     },\n26:     {\n27:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-87dZNOm\",\n28:       \"author\": {\n29:         \"login\": \"Caroline-99\"\n30:       },\n31:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n32:       \"body\": \"**Initial trial using the agent mode - it delegated the task to CL-curator **  \\n\\nI've completed the initial research and validation for the two new exhausted T cell terms. Here's what I found:\\n\\n### ✅ Validated Information\\n\\n**Literature Review:**\\n- Reviewed PMIDs 31390978, 31207603, 36907685, and 38166256\\n- **PD-1 is confirmed as a universal hallmark** across exhausted T cells\\n- **TOX is critical for CD8+ exhaustion** (PMID:31207603)\\n- The comment by @scheuerm is correct - \\\\\\\"as a result of\\\\\\\" is more accurate (already in the definitions)\\n\\n**Parent Term Placement - APPROVED:**\\n- CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell → CL:0000624 ✓\\n- CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell → CL:0000625 ✓\\n- Correctly NOT using CL:0011025 (exhausted T cell) as parent\\n\\n### ⚠️ Issue Identified\\n\\n**PMID:35880649 is INCORRECT** - This paper is about eye disease (nanophthalmos/retinitis pigmentosa), not T cell exhaustion. This reference should be removed or replaced.\\n\\n### 📦 Import Status\\n\\n**Required protein markers:**\\n- ✅ PD-1 (PR:000001919) - already in CL\\n- ✅ CD4, CD8, CD39, T-bet, EOMES - already in CL\\n- 📥 LAG-3, TIM-3, TOX - added to pr_terms.txt for import\\n\\n### 🎯 Next Steps\\n\\n1. Need to run protein import refresh command\\n2. Create the two new CL terms with:\\n   - New IDs in CL_99xxxxx range (as per idrange requirements)\\n   - Validated definitions (minus PMID:35880649)\\n   - Logical definitions using parent terms and markers\\n   - ORCID contributors added\\n\\n - Could you confirm if you want to proceed without PMID:35880649, or would you like to provide an alternative reference for epigenetic mechanisms in T cell exhaustion?\\n\\nSigned: GitHub Copilot\\\"\",\n33:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-01-06T11:34:25Z\",\n34:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n35:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n36:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n37:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n38:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3453#issuecomment-3714372518\",\n39:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n40:     },\n41:     {\n42:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-87dZRL1\",\n43:       \"author\": {\n44:         \"login\": \"Caroline-99\"\n45:       },\n46:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n47:       \"body\": \"**A trial assigning directly to CL-curator** \\n\\n---\\n\\n# Curation Report: CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell & CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n\\n**Issue**: #3453  \\n**Date**: 6 January 2026  \\n**Curator**: GitHub Copilot  \\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Term Identification\\n\\n**TWO TERMS REQUESTED:**\\n\\n### Term 1:\\n- **Proposed Label**: CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n- **Status**: New term (NTR)\\n- **Domain**: Cell Type - Immune Cell\\n\\n### Term 2:\\n- **Proposed Label**: CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n- **Status**: New term (NTR)\\n- **Domain**: Cell Type - Immune Cell\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Definition Validation\\n\\n### CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n\\n**Proposed Definition**: \\n\\nA CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation (e.g., chronic infection, tumors, or persistent inflammation). This state is characterized by sustained expression of PD-1 as a shared feature. Additional exhaustion-associated molecules, including the transcription factor TOX, and context- or stage-dependent changes in markers such as LAG-3, TIM-3, CD39, and T-bet, may also be observed; however, the expression levels of these molecules vary depending on exhaustion stage and tissue environment.\\n\\n**Literature Support**:\\n\\n- **PMID:31390978** - Dong et al. (2019) - \\\"CD4+ T cell exhaustion revealed by high PD-1 and LAG-3 expression and the loss of helper T cell function in chronic hepatitis B.\\\" \\n  - This paper directly demonstrates CD4+ T cell exhaustion in chronic HBV infection with high PD-1 and LAG-3 expression and impaired cytokine secretion (IFN-γ, IL-2, TNF-α).\\n  - DOI: 10.1186/s12865-019-0309-9\\n  - BMC Immunology, Open Access\\n\\n- **PMID:31207603** - Khan et al. (2019) - \\\"TOX transcriptionally and epigenetically programs CD8+ T cell exhaustion.\\\" \\n  - While focused on CD8+ T cells, this landmark Nature paper established TOX as a central regulator o... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n48:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-01-06T11:40:04Z\",\n49:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n50:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n51:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n52:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n53:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3453#issuecomment-3714388725\",\n54:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n55:     }\n56:   ],\n57:   \"title\": \"[NTR] CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell / CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\",\n58:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3453\"\n59: }\n\n(End of file - total 59 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\n- CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n- CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nCD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\n- exhausted CD4 T cell\\n- CD4+ exhausted T lymphocyte\\n- exhausted CD4-positive T cell\\n\\nCD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\n- exhausted CD8 T cell\\n- CD8+ exhausted T lymphocyte\\n- exhausted CD8-positive T cell\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nCD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\nA CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation(e.g., chronic infection, tumors, or persistent inflammation). This state is characterised by sustained expression of PD-1 as a shared feature. Additional exhaustion-associated molecules, including the transcription factor TOX, and context- or stage-dependent changes in markers such as LAG-3, TIM-3, CD39, and T-bet, may also be observed; however, the expression levels of these molecules vary depending on exhaustion stage and tissue environment.\\n(PMID:31390978; PMID:31207603; PMID:36907685; PMID:38166256)\\n\\nCD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell:\\nA CD8-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation (e.g., chronic infection, tumours, or persistent inflammation). This state is characterised by sustained expression of PD-1 as a shared feature. Additional exhaustion-associated molecules, including expression of the transcription factor TOX and reduced T-bet, and context- or stage-dependent changes in markers such as LAG-3, TIM-3, CD39, and EOMES, may also be observed; however, the expression levels of these molecules vary depending on exhaustion stage and disea... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-87UJcoB\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"scheuerm\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n      \"body\": \"Rather than \\\"A CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation under chronic antigenic stimulation\\\" I would recommend \\\"A CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation **_as a result_** of chronic antigenic stimulation\\\"\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-20T17:31:29Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"THUMBS_UP\",\n          \"users\": {\n            \"totalCount\": 1\n          }","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778976055067,"end":1778976055106}},"id":"prt_e333c5f0f001BN0HKe89oMZYOV","sessionID":"ses_1ccc3b105ffeGJVZ03NDbrWwnP","messageID":"msg_e333c501d001nS4LI3E5s866AG"}}
