{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778976132547,"sessionID":"ses_1ccc3b105ffeGJVZ03NDbrWwnP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5XiWt2XTLyzCU3qsEoLtwfl9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":35490,"limit":55},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n35490: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0020021))\n35491: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\n35492: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003328))\n35493: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003353))\n35494: \n35495: # Class: obo:CL_7770002 (juxtacanalicular tissue cell)\n35496: \n35497: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25356439\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770002 \"A trabecular meshwork cell of the juxtacanalicular tissue (JCT), characterized by a spindle-shaped, fibroblast-like morphology within a loose extracellular matrix immediately adjacent to Schlemm's canal. It expresses CHI3L1 (human and mouse) and ANGPTL7 (human), as well as smooth muscle actin for contractility. Unlike other trabecular meshwork cells, it does not form monolayers but exists in a loose network, regulating aqueous humor outflow resistance through continuous ECM remodelling, mechanotransduction, and formation of intracellular pores historically called giant vacuoles.\")\n35498: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_7770002 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3275\")\n35499: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_7770002 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35500: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_7770002 \"2025-01-29T08:52:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35501: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_7770002 \"JCT cell\")\n35502: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_7770002 \"juxtacanalicular tissue cell\")\n35503: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 obo:CL_0000327)\n35504: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 obo:CL_0002367)\n35505: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070278))\n35506: \n35507: # Class: obo:CL_7770003 (beam A cell)\n35508: \n35509: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27443500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770003 \"A beam cell within the eye's trabecular meshwork, molecularly distinguished by FABP4 expression in humans and spatially intermingled with Beam B cells throughout the uveal and corneoscleral meshwork regions. In mice, a transcriptionally analogous Beam A–like cluster (mC14) exists, sharing core TM markers (Myoc, Mgp, Pdpn, Chil1) and functional attributes.\")\n35510: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_7770003 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35511: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_7770003 \"2025-08-29T08:53:47Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35512: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_7770003 \"beam A cell\")\n35513: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35836364\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Trabecular meshwork (TM) structure. The TM consists of uveal (blue), corneoscleral (red), and juxtacanalicular (green) regions. TM beam cells (blue/red) line the uveal and corneoscleral regions, while JCT cells (green) occupy the juxtacanalicular region.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_7770003 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Trabecular_meshowk_cells_PMID35836364.jpg\")\n35514: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770003 obo:CL_7770005)\n35515: \n35516: # Class: obo:CL_7770004 (suprabasal cell)\n35517: \n35518: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17020902\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30837987\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32187560\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32726565\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37672481\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770004 \"An epithelial cell that resides in the layer(s) immediately above the basal layer in stratified or pseudostratified epithelia. This cell mainly originates from basal cells and is found across various tissues, including skin, esophagus, oral mucosa, airway, and cornea.\")\n35519: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_7770004 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35520: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_7770004 \"2025-09-05T07:59:28Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35521: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_7770004 \"suprabasal cell\")\n35522: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770004 obo:CL_0000066)\n35523: \n35524: # Class: obo:CL_7770005 (beam cell)\n35525: \n35526: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25356439\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27443500\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770005 \"A trabecular meshwork cell that is part of the eye's trabecular meshwork, residing in the uveal and corneoscleral meshwork regions and serving as the primary biological filter in the aqueous humor drainage cascade. This cell exhibits endothelial-like properties, including production of antithrombogenic substances such as tissue plasminogen activator, while also demonstrating phagocytic activity to remove cellular debris from aqueous humour before the fluid moves deeper into the less porous juxtacanalicular tissue.\")\n35527: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_7770005 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35528: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_7770005 \"2025-09-12T11:19:45Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35529: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_7770005 \"beam cell\")\n35530: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35836364\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Trabecular meshwork (TM) structure. The TM consists of uveal (blue), corneoscleral (red), and juxtacanalicular (green) regions. TM beam cells (blue/red) line the uveal and corneoscleral regions, while JCT cells (green) occupy the juxtacanalicular region.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_7770005 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Trabecular_meshowk_cells_PMID35836364.jpg\")\n35531: SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_7770005 obo:CL_0002367)\n35532: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770005 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0005969))\n35533: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770005 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0006909))\n35534: \n35535: # Class: obo:CL_7770006 (beam B cell, human)\n35536: \n35537: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25356439\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770006 \"A trabecular meshwork cell within the eye's trabecular meshwork. This cell is molecularly distinguished by TMEFF2 expression in humans. A beam B cell is spatially intermingled with beam A cells throughout the uveal and corneoscleral meshwork regions, but demonstrates a tendency to localise closer to the juxtacanalicular tissue.\")\n35538: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_7770006 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\n35539: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_7770006 \"2025-09-15T08:48:01Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35540: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_7770006 \"beam B cell, human\")\n35541: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35836364\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Trabecular meshwork (TM) structure. The TM consists of uveal (blue), corneoscleral (red), and juxtacanalicular (green) regions. TM beam cells (blue/red) line the uveal and corneoscleral regions, while JCT cells (green) occupy the juxtacanalicular region.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_7770006 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Trabecular_meshowk_cells_PMID35836364.jpg\")\n35542: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770006 obo:CL_0002367)\n35543: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606))\n35544: SubClassOf(obo:CL_7770006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9UIK5))\n\n(Showing lines 35490-35544 of 35625. Use offset=35545 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0020021))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003328))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003353))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_7770002 (juxtacanalicular tissue cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25356439\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770002 \"A trabecular meshwork cell of the juxtacanalicular tissue (JCT), characterized by a spindle-shaped, fibroblast-like morphology within a loose extracellular matrix immediately adjacent to Schlemm's canal. It expresses CHI3L1 (human and mouse) and ANGPTL7 (human), as well as smooth muscle actin for contractility. Unlike other trabecular meshwork cells, it does not form monolayers but exists in a loose network, regulating aqueous humor outflow resistance through continuous ECM remodelling, mechanotransduction, and formation of intracellular pores historically called giant vacuoles.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_7770002 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3275\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_7770002 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_7770002 \"2025-01-29T08:52:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_7770002 \"JCT cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_7770002 \"juxtacanalicular tissue cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 obo:CL_0000327)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 obo:CL_0002367)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_7770002 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070278))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_7770003 (beam A cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27443500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32341164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39829808\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_7770003 \"A beam cell within the eye's trabecular meshwork, molecularly distinguished by FABP4 expression in humans and spatially intermingled with Beam B cells throughout the uveal and corneoscleral meshwork regions. In mice, a transcriptionally analogous Beam A–like cluster (mC14) exists, sharing core TM markers (Myoc, Mgp, Pdpn, Chil1) and functional attributes.\")","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778976132476,"end":1778976132546}},"id":"prt_e333d8b09001HKtHHxHwVhPeQs","sessionID":"ses_1ccc3b105ffeGJVZ03NDbrWwnP","messageID":"msg_e333d85e1001o2zwF8XHCT9KAl"}}
