{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778976237124,"sessionID":"ses_1ccc3b105ffeGJVZ03NDbrWwnP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_Y2oFgXzFv7TL4S91aTSYqynm","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the requested CD4-positive and CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell terms. Changes committed locally and ready for PR #<NN>.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed issue #3453 by adding two new Cell Ontology terms:\n+\n+- `CL_9900001` CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\n+- `CL_9900002` CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Added definitions using the requested \"as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation\" wording.\n+- Added cited definition references from the issue and curator notes.\n+- Added exact synonyms for each term with literature xrefs.\n+- Placed the terms under the requested lineage parents, `CL_0000624` and `CL_0000625`.\n+- Added `CL_0011025` exhausted T cell as an additional superclass to preserve the exhaustion classification while keeping lineage-specific placement.\n+- Added PD-1 expression axioms using `RO_0002104 some PR_000001919`.\n+- Added contributor ORCIDs, creation dates, creator metadata, and issue tracker links.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The issue and follow-up curation notes supported adding both lineage-specific exhausted alpha-beta T cell subsets.\n+- The generic exhausted T cell term was not used as the sole parent because the requested terms are lineage-defined CD4/CD8 alpha-beta T cell subsets.\n+- PMID:35880649 was not used, in line with the curator note that it is unrelated to T cell exhaustion.\n+- Marker modeling was kept conservative: PD-1 was asserted because the issue identifies it as the shared required marker, while other context-dependent molecules were retained in the textual definitions rather than added as required logical axioms.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+\n+- Reviewed imported issue title, body, and comments.\n+- Checked existing CL terms for requested labels and placement terms.\n+- Confirmed existing PD-1 protein reference in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Edited only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` for ontology changes.\n+- Validated parsing with `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`.\n+- Committed only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` locally.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+Implemented the requested CD4-positive and CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell terms. Changes committed locally and ready for PR #<NN>.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+Addressed issue #3453 by adding two new Cell Ontology terms:\n+\n+- `CL_9900001` CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\n+- `CL_9900002` CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Added definitions using the requested \"as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation\" wording.\n+- Added cited definition references from the issue and curator notes.\n+- Added exact synonyms for each term with literature xrefs.\n+- Placed the terms under the requested lineage parents, `CL_0000624` and `CL_0000625`.\n+- Added `CL_0011025` exhausted T cell as an additional superclass to preserve the exhaustion classification while keeping lineage-specific placement.\n+- Added PD-1 expression axioms us